1
00:00:02,277 --> 00:00:05,245
Now I will not dive into all possible types

2
00:00:05,245 --> 00:00:07,250
we have. Instead, I wanna focus on a couple

3
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:08,341
of core features.

4
00:00:09,175 --> 00:00:11,453
Therefore, as a next step, let's add some

5
00:00:11,886 --> 00:00:14,356
configuration to this project so that I can

6
00:00:14,388 --> 00:00:16,602
briefly walk you through some core settings,

7
00:00:16,634 --> 00:00:18,045
especially one core setting.

8
00:00:18,639 --> 00:00:20,933
We can add a configuration file which will

9
00:00:20,965 --> 00:00:22,874
then be taken into account by the TypeScript

10
00:00:22,874 --> 00:00:26,740
compiler to this project by running tsc

11
00:00:26,980 --> 00:00:27,301
--init.

12
00:00:28,022 --> 00:00:30,218
This adds a tsconfig.json file

13
00:00:30,907 --> 00:00:32,701
which has quite a lot of options you can

14
00:00:32,749 --> 00:00:33,102
set.

15
00:00:34,111 --> 00:00:35,105
Now you can

16
00:00:35,938 --> 00:00:38,518
read through these comments here. I do talk

17
00:00:38,518 --> 00:00:40,697
about the options in greater detail in my

18
00:00:41,467 --> 00:00:42,909
Understanding TypeScript course.

19
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:46,642
Here I will leave most options as they are,

20
00:00:47,155 --> 00:00:48,966
so I will not comment them in,

21
00:00:49,575 --> 00:00:52,187
but I want to talk about this strict option

22
00:00:52,219 --> 00:00:55,154
because that is important. Strict mode is

23
00:00:55,331 --> 00:00:56,728
generally encouraged.

24
00:00:57,259 --> 00:00:59,813
It means that certain things are not allowed

25
00:00:59,845 --> 00:01:01,789
which normally would be allowed in

26
00:01:01,837 --> 00:01:02,255
TypeScript.

27
00:01:02,994 --> 00:01:05,371
And we see this in our app.ts file. Just by

28
00:01:05,371 --> 00:01:07,444
adding this configuration, I now get an

29
00:01:07,476 --> 00:01:07,829
error here

30
00:01:08,601 --> 00:01:09,918
that this is possibly null.

31
00:01:10,753 --> 00:01:12,858
This is one strict mode feature.

32
00:01:13,565 --> 00:01:16,360
We have this strict null check which is

33
00:01:16,392 --> 00:01:19,605
turned on. All those checks here are turned

34
00:01:19,685 --> 00:01:22,063
on if strict is set to true. Alternatively,

35
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:24,682
you comment out this line and just comment

36
00:01:24,730 --> 00:01:25,228
in the

37
00:01:25,774 --> 00:01:27,011
features you want down there.

38
00:01:27,734 --> 00:01:29,774
So they're all set to true when setting

39
00:01:29,806 --> 00:01:30,529
strict to true,

40
00:01:31,075 --> 00:01:33,003
and one of these features ensures that

41
00:01:33,003 --> 00:01:34,593
you're not calling something

42
00:01:35,172 --> 00:01:36,987
on something else which might be null.

43
00:01:37,919 --> 00:01:38,770
And here indeed,

44
00:01:39,846 --> 00:01:42,642
we select a button, but of course TypeScript

45
00:01:42,642 --> 00:01:44,714
can't know whether that button actually

46
00:01:44,810 --> 00:01:48,409
exists. It does not check our HTML code.

47
00:01:49,242 --> 00:01:51,245
So therefore, this could be null if we don't

48
00:01:51,245 --> 00:01:53,537
find a button, if we have no button element.

49
00:01:54,594 --> 00:01:56,901
Now to work around this, we have 2 options.

50
00:01:57,574 --> 00:01:59,369
We can add some code here

51
00:02:00,138 --> 00:02:03,070
where we check if button element is truthy

52
00:02:04,128 --> 00:02:04,272
and

53
00:02:04,945 --> 00:02:06,883
move that code into that if check.

54
00:02:07,412 --> 00:02:09,976
Now we know that if this code runs, button

55
00:02:09,976 --> 00:02:11,226
element can't be null

56
00:02:12,235 --> 00:02:14,238
because if it would be null, it would be

57
00:02:14,238 --> 00:02:16,305
falsy and we wouldn't make it into this if

58
00:02:16,321 --> 00:02:16,513
check.

59
00:02:17,909 --> 00:02:18,696
Alternatively,

60
00:02:19,354 --> 00:02:19,851
we know

61
00:02:20,558 --> 00:02:23,030
that there will be a button, just as we know

62
00:02:23,302 --> 00:02:25,951
that these elements here are HTML input

63
00:02:25,951 --> 00:02:26,320
elements.

64
00:02:27,074 --> 00:02:28,086
In such cases,

65
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:30,879
we can add an exclamation mark here.

66
00:02:32,131 --> 00:02:32,981
This simply means

67
00:02:33,736 --> 00:02:35,694
the statement in front of it, the expression

68
00:02:35,726 --> 00:02:36,288
in front of it,

69
00:02:36,850 --> 00:02:38,968
could theoretically be null, but we know

70
00:02:38,968 --> 00:02:39,562
that it isn't.

71
00:02:40,333 --> 00:02:43,366
So please, TypeScript, ignore that null case

72
00:02:43,447 --> 00:02:46,249
and take the other value. In this case, take

73
00:02:46,410 --> 00:02:49,109
HTML button element as the only value.

74
00:02:50,289 --> 00:02:50,564
This

75
00:02:51,097 --> 00:02:52,794
is important and that's something I wanted

76
00:02:52,794 --> 00:02:53,522
to show you here.

77
00:02:55,540 --> 00:02:57,017
One other thing that wouldn't be allowed

78
00:02:57,017 --> 00:03:00,200
with strict mode is that you omit the type

79
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:01,710
of one parameter, for example.

80
00:03:02,392 --> 00:03:04,758
Now it complains that this parameter

81
00:03:04,888 --> 00:03:06,634
implicitly has the any type.

82
00:03:07,475 --> 00:03:09,965
There is an any type which you can assign

83
00:03:10,305 --> 00:03:12,747
and that also is fine, but that's a very

84
00:03:12,811 --> 00:03:15,434
generic fallback type. It basically carries

85
00:03:15,530 --> 00:03:18,710
no extra type information. Any kind of value

86
00:03:18,903 --> 00:03:19,834
is allowed here.

87
00:03:20,445 --> 00:03:22,292
And therefore, this is really just the type

88
00:03:22,292 --> 00:03:24,589
you should know if you have no idea which

89
00:03:24,685 --> 00:03:27,158
kind of data you can expect. If you do know

90
00:03:27,190 --> 00:03:29,728
it better, it is recommended that you are as

91
00:03:29,824 --> 00:03:32,185
clear as possible. In this case, that you

92
00:03:32,185 --> 00:03:34,016
simply define that you want a number.

93
00:03:34,819 --> 00:03:37,052
But even if you don't know it, if you set

94
00:03:37,052 --> 00:03:38,272
this to any, it's okay.

95
00:03:38,915 --> 00:03:41,420
But not setting any type That's not

96
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:42,897
something the strict mode allows.

97
00:03:43,492 --> 00:03:46,109
Because then this is implicitly any but it

98
00:03:46,125 --> 00:03:48,598
looks like you simply forgot to look into

99
00:03:48,614 --> 00:03:50,556
this argument. And you should at least

100
00:03:50,556 --> 00:03:53,158
explicitly set any to make it very clear

101
00:03:53,206 --> 00:03:55,117
that you don't know better or that you

102
00:03:55,133 --> 00:03:57,734
indeed want to allow any kind of value here.

103
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:01,041
So explicit any is allowed, implicit any

104
00:04:01,138 --> 00:04:03,498
isn't and it's even better if you set the

105
00:04:03,498 --> 00:04:05,746
specific type you are expecting.

106
00:04:06,452 --> 00:04:08,695
Now important, as soon as you added a

107
00:04:08,695 --> 00:04:10,329
tsconfig.json file,

108
00:04:11,002 --> 00:04:12,893
once you run the TypeScript compiler, you

109
00:04:13,005 --> 00:04:14,816
can still select the file,

110
00:04:15,409 --> 00:04:18,197
but then the tsconfig.json configuration

111
00:04:18,213 --> 00:04:19,831
will not be taken into account.

112
00:04:20,552 --> 00:04:22,395
Instead, as soon as you do have such a

113
00:04:22,395 --> 00:04:23,869
tsconfig.json file,

114
00:04:24,622 --> 00:04:26,176
just run tsc like this

115
00:04:26,721 --> 00:04:29,173
and it will compile all TypeScript files in

116
00:04:29,285 --> 00:04:29,958
the folder

117
00:04:30,647 --> 00:04:33,627
whilst taking the config file into account.

118
00:04:34,253 --> 00:04:36,615
So only if you don't point at a specific

119
00:04:36,663 --> 00:04:39,234
file, the configuration file will be taken

120
00:04:39,234 --> 00:04:41,966
into account and all TypeScript files in the

121
00:04:41,966 --> 00:04:43,219
folder will be configured.

122
00:04:43,894 --> 00:04:46,207
You can still target the file if you want

123
00:04:46,207 --> 00:04:48,762
to, then the configuration file is ignored

124
00:04:48,794 --> 00:04:50,931
for the TypeScript compilation though. The

125
00:04:51,028 --> 00:04:51,205
IDE

126
00:04:52,072 --> 00:04:54,707
always picks up the config.json file, so the

127
00:04:54,723 --> 00:04:57,889
IDE support is always provided no matter how

128
00:04:57,937 --> 00:04:58,805
you then compile it.
